                                "sense_id": "05b434e8-a375-325b-b866-4e51b21641c4",
                                "text": "There is also one of the woodblocks used to print Jacopo de’ Barbari’s revolutionary bird’s-eye panorama of Venice and the lagoon, from 1500."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cf9e26d-234a-4ecc-a0b6-dff402139569",
                                "sense_id": "05b434e8-a375-325b-b866-4e51b21641c4",
                                "text": "In the 1970s Thiebaud became increasingly interested in landscapes and cityscapes that he painted from a bird’s-eye perspective. In “Potrero Hill” a painting from the mid-1970s, he jammed freeways, hills and buildings together in a steep vertical of color and light."
                            }
